cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "OptiArchitect: a bilingual, verification-first toolkit for teaching operations research"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmarAl-Zuabidi/OptiArchitect-Suite"
url: "https://github.com/OmarAl-Zuabidi/OptiArchitect-Suite"
abstract: >-
  OptiArchitect is an open-source Python toolkit that teaches the core algorithms of
  operations research (simplex variants, transportation and assignment problems, and
  single-variable non-linear optimization) while verifying every answer it produces.
  It offers an interactive English/Arabic console, a Streamlit web application and a
  Python API on one shared solver core.
